Common options you’ll actually use

--m3u – write an M3U file alongside your downloads.

--archive my_archive.txt – keep a list of what you’ve already grabbed to avoid duplicates.

--scan-for-songs + --overwrite skip/force – control how SpotDL treats files you already have.

--playlist-numbering – embed playlist order in track numbers/album tagging. 
spotDL

How it organizes your files

By default, SpotDL writes neatly tagged audio and cover images. Because tags come from Spotify while audio comes from YouTube, you usually get clean filenames and library-ready tags with minimal fuss. Recent releases even improved lyrics handling, per-track art with playlist numbering, and duplicate-skipping. 
